From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] di_multi: di_que_list: drain a local kfifo copy

di_que_list() snapshots a queue by memcpy'ing the live struct kfifo header
of fifo[qtype] into the per-channel fifo[QUE_DBG], then drains that copy
with an unbounded while (kfifo_out()) loop.

After the first call fifo[QUE_DBG].data aliases fifo[qtype].data, so the
buffer di_que_alloc() gave QUE_DBG leaks and di_que_release() later
kfifo_free()s the same buffer twice. fifo[QUE_DBG] is also unlocked shared
state: a debug lister racing the DI task can retear in/out mid-drain and
run the loop past the caller's arr[MAX_FIFO_SIZE + 1] on the stack.

Copy the header into a local struct kfifo, drain that, stop at
MAX_FIFO_SIZE entries, and report *rsize as the count actually copied.
With no concurrent writer the output is identical to before.

Not exercised on hardware.

--- a/drivers/media/di_multi/di_que.c
+++ b/drivers/media/di_multi/di_que.c
@@ -186,6 +186,7 @@
 {
 	struct di_ch_s *pch = get_chdata(ch);
 /*	unsigned int tmp[MAX_FIFO_SIZE + 1];*/
+	struct kfifo tmp_fifo;
 	int i;
 	unsigned int index;
 	bool ret = false;
@@ -201,8 +202,11 @@
 	}
 
 	ret = true;
-	memcpy(&pch->fifo[QUE_DBG], &pch->fifo[qtype],
-	       sizeof(pch->fifo[qtype]));
+	/*
+	 * drain a local copy: fifo[QUE_DBG] owns its own buffer and
+	 * would be shared by concurrent listers
+	 */
+	tmp_fifo = pch->fifo[qtype];
 
 #ifdef MARK_HIS
 	if (kfifo_is_empty(&pbm->fifo[QUE_DBG]))
@@ -212,13 +216,15 @@
 	i = 0;
 	*rsize = 0;
 
-	while (kfifo_out(&pch->fifo[QUE_DBG], &index, sizeof(unsigned int))
+	while (i < MAX_FIFO_SIZE &&
+	       kfifo_out(&tmp_fifo, &index, sizeof(unsigned int))
 		== sizeof(unsigned int)) {
 		outbuf[i] = index;
 		/*pr_info("%d->%d\n",i,index);*/
 		i++;
 	}
-	*rsize = di_que_list_count(ch, qtype);
+	/* entries actually copied, never more than outbuf holds */
+	*rsize = i;
 	#ifdef MARK_HIS	/*debug only*/
 	que_dbg("%s: size[%d]\n", di_name_new_que[qtype], *rsize);
 	for (i = 0; i < *rsize; i++)
